# Binary geo tables (06-04). `prettier --check .` walks the whole tree and
# fails on a file it has no parser for, so the container and its fixtures are
# excluded here rather than renamed to dodge the check.
**/*.bin
# The generated world map (06-07). One object per line, each carrying a
# multi-hundred-character SVG path, so Prettier would either reflow 238 lines
# into an unreadable diff or wrap every path across three. tsc and ESLint still
# cover the file; only the formatter stands down.
src/lib/geo/world-map.generated.ts
# The generated tank table (13-02). Every string is written with JSON.stringify
# so a quote in a vehicle name can never break the module, which means the file
# uses double quotes where Prettier would use single ones — and Prettier would
# rewrite it, so `pnpm run vehicles:table:check` would then fail against a file
# Prettier had edited. tsc and ESLint still cover the file; only the formatter
# stands down.
src/lib/features/overview/vehicle-table.generated.ts
